      "writtenOn": "2025-06-13T22:59:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This loop seems like it has excessive lock traffic for what you\u0027re trying to do? What if instead of unlocking + relocking for each node, we did (very very pseudo-code)\n\n```\nloop {\nlet mut count;\nlock()\ncount \u003d /* iterate nodes and count */;\nif count \u003c\u003d batch.capacity() {\n  /* iterate nodes and fill batch out */\n  return batch;\n}\nunlock()\nbatch.reserve(count)?;\nprealloc.reserve(count)?;\nfor _ in prealloc.len()..prealloc.capacity() {\n  prealloc.push(ArcUnique::new_uninit())?;\n}\n}\n```\n\nThis would mean that in the \"good\" case (your initial vectors are big enough), you\u0027d lock and unlock once, but still keep all the allocations outside the lock. This also avoids the calls to `cursor_lower_bound`, because you don\u0027t need to do an intermediate unlock.",
      "revId": "a0d9beadb09117305a75cd6503e4c34c02db9acc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
